    "media:imagetext": "Cocktails\nUNITED'S VERY DRY BEEFEATER MARTINI\nUNITED'S VERY DRY SMIRNOFF SILVER VODKA MARTINI\nOLD FASHIONED MANHATTAN SCREWDRIVER\nBLOODY MARY MAI TAI\nWHISKEY SOUR\n1.50\nSpirits\nOLD GRAND DAD BOURBON\nDEWAR'S WHITE LABEL SCOTCH\nCHIVAS REGAL SCOTCH\nCANADIAN CLUB\nJACK DANIELS TENNESSEE WHISKEY\nBEEFEATER GIN\nSMIRNOFF VODKA BACARDI RUM\nCHRISTIAN BROTHERS BRANDY\n1.50\nLiqueurs\nBENEDICTINE AND BRANDY\nCOGNAC\nGRAND MARNIER\n1.50\nCREME DE MENTHE\nGALLIANO\nWines and Beer\nCHAMPAGNE\nDRY SACK SHERRY\nRED WINE\nWHITE WINE\n1.00\nDOMESTIC BEER\n.50\nCOMPLIMENTARY SOFT BEVERAGES\nMinors Will Not Be Served Liquor.\nHawaii\nLittle\nCorner\nSalad\nCOMBINATION SALAD, GREEN GODDESS DRESSING\nYour Choice of\nPEPPER BEEF\nChoice beef is well seasoned, braised with sliced onion, red and\ngreen bell peppers and served with a spicy Pepper Sauce.\nBUTTERED NOODLES\nCARROTS VICHY\nor\nTHE CHEF'S FRIEND SHIP SPECIALTY\nBRAISED PORK CHOPS WESTMORELAND\nCenter cut pork chops are seasoned and sauteed\nto a golden brown.\nBUTTERED BRUSSEL SPROUTS\nCARROTS VICHY\nor\nFROM THE KITCHENS OF YOUR LAND\nPrepared from an original early American recipe, today's\nrevolutionary dish is a delicious part of our heritage. You\nwill find it described on the enclosed menu card along with\nsome interesting, perhaps less known, facts and fun about\nfood during our short, proud 200 years.\nSavor a bit of history - We're sure you'll enjoy it.\nDINNER ROLL\nBUTTER PAT\nDESSERT\nBeverages\nCOFFEE SANKA\nTEA\nMILK\nThis menu prepared in United Airlines Flight Kitchen\nat Portland,\nErich Dorfhuber, Executive Chef.\nMember, Chef's De Cuisine Society of Oregon.\nPlease accept our apology if your choice is not available.\nPDXHH\nL/D2-4",
